  m_Name: EntanglementTutorial02
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::QC.Systems.Tutorials.TutorialSequenceSO
  tutorialId: ent02
  steps:
  - headerText: Entangling Objects
    bodyText: 'There are some objects here that you can interact with: a green moving
      box, a gray box which you can move by pushing it and a rotating gear.


      Go
      ahead and press the "Q" button on your keyboard to go into Entanglement Mode!'
    illustrationMode: 0
    illustration: {fileID: 0}
    flipbookFrames: []
    flipbookFrameRate: 12
    highlightMode: 0
    highlightTargetId: 
    worldHighlightRadius: 60
    advanceMode: 1
    requiredEventName: entanglementModeToggled
    timerSeconds: 0
  - headerText: Entangling Objects
    bodyText: 'In entanglement mode, objects which can be entangled are marked by
      red selectors. When entanglement mode is turned on, there are no selected objects.


      In
      order to select an object, simply Left Click with your mouse hovering over
      it. The red selector will turn green to indicate that that object is selected.


      If
      you have an object selected already, clicking on a different object will entangle
      the two objects. The object you clicked first will affect the second one. In
      that way, the first object is considered a "Source" and the second one is considered
      a "Partner".


      Sources can affect Partners but not the other way around.'
    illustrationMode: 0
    illustration: {fileID: 0}
    flipbookFrames: []
    flipbookFrameRate: 23.976
    highlightMode: 2
    highlightTargetId: TutorialMovingPlatform
    worldHighlightRadius: 60
    advanceMode: 0
    requiredEventName: 
    timerSeconds: 0
  - headerText: Entangling Objects
    bodyText: 'Before moving on to the next section, spend some time here to get
      used to the feel of entangling objects.


      When you feel you have gotten
      the hang of it, proceed to the next section.'
    illustrationMode: 0
    illustration: {fileID: 0}
